Interior illustration of a Mediterranean noble dining room in elegant decline. Perspective view from the doorway looking in.

SCENE: A rectangular dining room, evening. Warm candlelight from an iron chandelier (half the candles missing). A large fireplace on the left wall, fire lit, casting orange glow. Two tall windows on the far wall show a dark garden with cypress silhouettes.

TABLE: Rectangular wooden table set for five. White tablecloth (slightly yellowed). Ceramic plates, simple but quality. A bottle of red wine, glasses half-full. Remains of pizza — thin crust, tomato, olives. Bread basket. Nothing lavish, but dignified.

ROOM DETAILS: Faded floral wallpaper, peeling slightly in the corners. A wooden sideboard against the right wall with more wine bottles and a tarnished silver candelabra. Paintings on the walls — landscapes in ornate frames (the frames are worth more than the paintings). The floor is terracotta tile, worn smooth. One rug under the table, threadbare but once expensive.

ATMOSPHERE: The room tells a story of wealth that's slowly draining away. Everything is quality — but nothing is new. The furniture is solid oak but scratched. The chandelier is iron but missing arms. The wallpaper was expensive but that was twenty years ago. Someone is trying to maintain dignity on a shrinking budget.

LIGHTING: Warm, intimate. Fireplace glow from the left, candles from above, moonlight through the windows. Shadows in the corners.

STYLE: Realistic fantasy illustration, painterly, warm color palette (amber, burgundy, cream, dark wood). No characters visible — the room is set and waiting. Slight melancholy. Think "a dinner party at a palazzo that's seen better days."

MOOD: Inviting but slightly unsettling. Beautiful but sad. The kind of room where secrets are shared over wine.
